      "number": 64728,
      "title": "Cache undefined widening properties per symbol, not per name",
      "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/pull/64728",
      "author": "maschwenk",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-18T04:59:09Z",
      "labels": [
        "For Uncommitted Bug"
      ],
      "hint": "unknown",
      "release": "⏳ 未リリース",
      "body": "Fixes #64727\n\ngetUndefinedProperty cached the synthetic `prop?: undefined` symbol by name, so the first object literal to widen a name decided how that property printed in later, unrelated types. declaration output then depended on which other files shared a checker, and on --checkers.\n\nthis keys the cache by the source property symbol instead. it's a 4 line change in checker.go.\n\n- new test undefinedPropertyDeclarationOrder covers the a.ts/b.ts repro\n- objectLiteralNormalization baselines reorder: c3, c4 and e2 now match 6.0.3 exactly, nothing moves further from it\n- emitted b.d.ts is byte-identical with and without a.ts at --checkers 1, 2, 4 and 8. before the fix it differed at 1, 2 and 4\n- hereby validate passes except test:extension, which fails the same way on clean main\n\nai disclosure: written with claude code. i've read the change and will handle review myself.",
